    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d535-a8">

                <pb facs="0948" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg852"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 8—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Panaman Commissioners to the American
                        Commissioners</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: Referring to Article XII of the treaty
                    signed by us today with the American Commission, in which arrangement is made to
                    make the subsidiary silver currency issued by the Republic of Panama legal
                    tender in the Canal Zone under certain conditions, we desire to state that the
                    Republic of Panama will cause the silver currency referred to in said Article to
                    be coined at one of the mints of the United States.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. J.Alfaro</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eusebio A. Morales</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
